# FlowDeploy — Backend (Go) Conventions

> **Stack**: Go 1.24, Fiber v2, pgx/v5 via `database/sql`, golang-migrate, google.golang.org/grpc, google/wire, swaggo/swag, log/slog (with `lmittmann/tint` for human formatting).
>
> Module: `github.com/paasdeploy/backend`. Subordinate to `flowdeploy-development-protocol.mdc`.

---

## 1. Directory Layout

```
apps/backend/
  cmd/api/                Application entrypoint (main.go)
  internal/
    config/               Env-driven Config struct (single source of truth)
    database/             Migration runner (golang-migrate)
    di/                   google/wire providers + wire_gen.go
    domain/               Pure domain types + repository interfaces (NO infra deps)
    repository/           Postgres implementations of domain.*Repository
    service/              Business logic that orchestrates repos and external clients
    handler/              Fiber HTTP handlers (thin)
    middleware/           Auth, trace
    response/             Response envelope helpers (response.OK/Created/BadRequest/...)
    requestctx/           Helpers to set/get user, traceId on fiber.Ctx
    engine/               Deploy engine: queue, dispatcher, worker, monitors, notifier
    grpcserver/           Backend-side gRPC server (agent registration, command bus)
    agentclient/          gRPC client to remote agents (with retry, pool, health)
    pki/                  Internal CA + per-agent cert generation (mTLS)
    crypto/               Token hashing, env var encryption helpers
    webhook/              GitHub webhook ingestion + signature verification
    ghclient/             GitHub REST/App client
    github/               GitHub OAuth flow
    cloudflare/           Cloudflare DNS API client
    notification/         Email / Slack / Discord senders
    provisioner/          SSH-based agent installation on a remote host
    sysinfo/              Local host metrics for the control plane
    server/               Fiber app construction, route registration helpers
    docs/                 Swagger DTOs (separate from domain to keep public API stable)
  gen/go/flowdeploy/v1/   Generated protobuf — DO NOT EDIT
  migrations/             SQL migrations (NNNNNN_*.up.sql / .down.sql)
  scripts/lint-go.sh      Lint runner (local + Docker)
  Dockerfile              Production multi-stage build
```

---

## 2. Layering

| Layer        | Responsibility                                                                 | May import                                    |
| ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------- |
| `domain`     | Pure types, status enums (`AppStatus`, `DeployStatus`), repository interfaces  | std lib only                                  |
| `repository` | SQL queries via `*sql.DB`; map rows → domain types                             | `domain`, `database/sql`, `pgx` driver        |
| `service`    | Business orchestration; calls repos, agent client, ghclient, webhook manager   | `domain`, `repository` (as interface), other services in same module, external clients |
| `handler`    | Fiber routing + auth guard + body parsing + response envelope                  | `service`, `response`, `requestctx`, `domain` (types only) |
| `engine`     | Long-lived workers: queue dispatcher, deploy worker, monitors                  | `domain`, `repository`, `service`, `agentclient`, `shared/pkg/*` |
| `grpcserver` | Agent registration, heartbeat, push commands                                   | generated `pb`, `service`, `domain`, `pki`    |
| `middleware` | Cross-cutting concerns (auth, trace)                                           | `domain`, `crypto`, `requestctx`, `response`  |

Hard rules:

- `handler` MUST NOT import `repository`. Always go through `service`.
- `repository` MUST NOT import `service` or `handler`.
- `domain` MUST NOT import any other internal package — it is the bottom of the stack.
- Generated `gen/go/...` is consumed by `engine`, `grpcserver`, `agentclient` — never by `handler` directly.

---

## 3. Configuration

`internal/config/config.go` is the single source of truth. Add a new env var by:

1. Extending the appropriate sub-struct (`ServerConfig`, `DeployConfig`, `GRPCConfig`, ...).
2. Reading it in `Load()` with a `getEnv*` helper and a sensible default.
3. Documenting it in `.env.example` (root) — do NOT touch `.env`.
4. If user-facing, mention it in `README.md`.

Defaults live as `const Default*` next to the struct. Never read `os.Getenv` outside `config/`.

---

## 4. HTTP Handlers (thin)

Rules:

- A handler method has at most ~20 lines — parse → guard → call service → respond.
- Authentication: pull `*domain.User` from context via `GetUserFromContext(c)` (in handler helpers) or `requestctx.User(c)`. Return `response.Unauthorized` if absent (`MsgNotAuthenticated`).
- Authorization: use `RequireAdminForLocal(c, serverID)` and similar role guards already defined in `handler/`. Do not implement ad-hoc role checks.
- Body parsing: `c.BodyParser(&input)` then `response.BadRequest(c, MsgInvalidRequestBody)` on error.
- Always go through `response.*` helpers. Never `c.Status(...).JSON(...)` by hand — the envelope (`{ success, data, error, meta }`) must be uniform.
- HTTP status correctness:
  - `200` for read, full update, idempotent action
  - `201` for create
  - `202` for accepted-async (e.g. enqueued deploy)
  - `204` for delete with no body
  - `400/401/403/404/409/429/500` via the matching `response.*` helper

Example (existing pattern in `app_handler.go`):

```go
func (h *AppHandler) ListApps(c *fiber.Ctx) error {
    user, err := h.requireAuth(c)
    if err != nil {
        return err
    }
    apps, err := h.appService.ListAppsWithDeployments(user.ID)
    if err != nil {
        return h.handleError(c, err)
    }
    return response.OK(c, apps)
}
```

Swagger:

- Annotate every public route with `@Summary`, `@Description`, `@Tags`, `@Produce`/`@Accept`, `@Success`, `@Failure`, `@Router`.
- Reference DTOs from `internal/docs/` (not `domain/`). Keep the `internal/docs/` schema stable; treat it as the published OpenAPI contract.
- Regenerate with `swag init` if you change annotations (the DI Wire generator is independent).

---

## 5. Services

- One file per aggregate (`app_service.go`, `audit_service.go`, `notification_service.go`).
- Constructors take dependencies as interfaces (typically `domain.*Repository`) plus loggers and external clients. Wire them via `internal/di/providers*.go`.
- Methods take `context.Context` for anything that touches IO.
- Return wrapped errors: `fmt.Errorf("create app: %w", err)`. Use `errors.Is` / `errors.As` upstream.
- Never expose internal SQL errors directly — translate to `domain.ErrNotFound`, `domain.ErrConflict`, etc. The handler maps domain errors to the right HTTP envelope (see `handler.handleError`).

---

## 6. Repositories

- One repository per aggregate, named `Postgres{Aggregate}Repository`, implementing the matching `domain.{Aggregate}Repository` interface.
- Reuse the column constants pattern (`appSelectColumns`) and the `appScanFields`/`scanDest()`/`toApp()` triplet to keep scanning DRY (see `repository/app_repository.go`).
- Always use parameterized queries. Never concatenate user input. Use `sql_helpers.go` for shared helpers (e.g. for `IN ($1, $2, ...)` builders).
- Map `sql.ErrNoRows` to `domain.ErrNotFound`.
- Never expose `*sql.DB` to upper layers — pass repo interfaces.

---

## 7. Engine (Deploy Workers)

`internal/engine/` is the long-lived worker subsystem. Files of note:

- `engine.go` — top-level `Engine` struct holds workers, monitors, dispatcher, notifier.
- `queue.go` — Postgres-backed FIFO using `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED`.
- `dispatcher.go` — pulls tasks from queue and hands them to workers.
- `worker.go` — single deploy executor unit; fan-out controlled by `DEPLOY_WORKERS`.
- `health_monitor.go`, `stats_monitor.go`, `system_stats_monitor.go`, `server_stats_monitor.go` — periodic background loops.
- `notifier.go` — broadcasts events to SSE consumers (handled by the SSE handler).

Rules:

- All loops respect `ctx.Done()`. `cancel()` is called from `main.go`'s shutdown sequence.
- Workers MUST be safe to crash mid-deploy. Use the lock package (`shared/pkg/lock`) and idempotent steps; never assume a previous step completed without re-checking state.
- Notification publishing is fire-and-forget on a buffered channel (size 1000). Don't block deploy progress on notifier back-pressure.
- Deploys to remote servers go through `agentclient` (gRPC). Local deploys use `shared/pkg/docker` and `shared/pkg/compose` directly.

---

## 8. Agent Client

`internal/agentclient/` wraps the gRPC client with:

- A connection pool (`conn_pool.go`) keyed by server ID.
- Health checking (`health_checker.go`).
- Retry policy (`retry.go`) — exponential backoff with jitter; only retry idempotent calls.
- Per-domain files split by responsibility (`agent_client_deploy.go`, `agent_client_containers.go`, `agent_client_images.go`, `agent_client_ssl.go`, `agent_client_system.go`, `agent_client_update.go`).

Rules:

- mTLS is mandatory. The client loads the agent's cert (provisioned by `pki/`) and the CA. `GRPCConfig.AgentTLSInsecureSkipVerify` exists for emergency recovery only and must NEVER default to true.
- Treat every remote call as fallible. Always set a deadline via `context.WithTimeout`.
- Never expose `*grpc.ClientConn` outside the package.

---

## 9. PKI

`internal/pki/ca.go` is the internal certificate authority that issues per-agent certs.

- Backed by data persisted via `domain.CertificateAuthorityRepository` (migration `000014_pki_ca`).
- `NewCA()` generates a fresh CA in tests; `LoadCA(certPEM, keyPEM)` rehydrates from storage.
- `GenerateAgentCert(serverID, host)` issues short-lived certs with the server ID embedded in CN/SAN — used by both backend (issuance) and agent (validation).
- DO NOT change the issuance algorithm or validity period without an ADR.

---

## 10. Authentication

- HTTP cookies: opaque session tokens stored in cookie `flowdeploy_session` (configurable via `SESSION_COOKIE_NAME`). Hashed via `crypto.HashSessionToken` and stored in `sessions` table.
- `middleware.AuthMiddleware.Require()` enforces auth. `Optional()` populates context if a valid session exists but does not block.
- GitHub OAuth lives in `internal/github/`; GitHub App (for repo access) in `internal/ghclient/`.
- Roles: `admin` and `user` (migration `000024`). `RequireAdminForLocal` blocks regular users from operating on the local host.

---

## 11. Migrations

- Tool: `golang-migrate`. Files at `apps/backend/migrations/` named `NNNNNN_description.{up,down}.sql`.
- Numbering is strictly sequential. NEVER renumber existing migrations or rewrite a published migration in place. Add a new one.
- Every `up` MUST have a corresponding `down`. The `down` should be a real best-effort rollback, not a stub.
- Migrations run automatically on backend boot via `runMigrationsFirst()` in `cmd/api/main.go`. Keep them idempotent-friendly (`IF NOT EXISTS` where it makes sense, but NEVER replace `CREATE TABLE` with `IF NOT EXISTS` to mask drift).

---

## 12. Logging and Errors

- Logger: `log/slog` configured with `lmittmann/tint` for human-readable output.
- Use structured fields: `logger.Info("agent registered", "server_id", id, "version", v)`. Never `Sprintf` into the message.
- Never log secrets, tokens, full env values, or webhook payloads with sensitive data.
- Wrap errors with context (`fmt.Errorf("operation X: %w", err)`). Don't log AND return the same error from the same layer — pick one site to log.

---

## 13. Dependency Injection (Wire)

- All wiring lives in `internal/di/`. `wire.go` declares the injector; `wire_gen.go` is generated — do not edit.
- Providers are split by concern: `providers.go`, `providers_db.go`, `providers_handlers.go`, `providers_engine.go`, `providers_auth.go`.
- After adding a new provider or constructor signature, run `go generate ./internal/di/...` (or `wire ./internal/di/...`) to regenerate `wire_gen.go`.
- Constructors must return `(*T, error)` if they can fail at startup. Wire will surface errors as a startup `panic` — the user sees them immediately.

---

## 14. gRPC Server (Backend Side)

`internal/grpcserver/` exposes a minimal control-plane gRPC service used by agents to:

1. `Register` — first contact, sends system info; backend issues mTLS cert.
2. `Heartbeat` — periodic; carries Docker info and basic metrics.
3. Receive commands pushed via the bidirectional command stream (`hub.go`, `commands.go`).

Rules:

- Register/Heartbeat may be called over TLS without client cert during the bootstrap window (provisioning). After registration, all calls must use mTLS.
- The hub is the single fan-out point for control plane → agent push. Use it; do not spawn ad-hoc streams.

---

## 15. Tests

Existing tested packages (use them as reference):

- `internal/pki/ca_test.go` — pure-function style.
- `internal/handler/template_handler_test.go` — handler-level test.
- `internal/provisioner/provisioner_test.go`.
- `internal/ghclient/{webhook,signature}_test.go`.
- `internal/webhook/github_manager_test.go`.

Conventions:

- Standard library testing only (no testify). Failures via `t.Fatalf`/`t.Errorf` with descriptive messages.
- Test names: `TestSubject_Behavior_Condition` (e.g. `TestRegister_RejectsExpiredCert`). All test descriptions in English.
- Table-driven tests for parsers/validators (see `ghclient/signature_test.go` style).
- Integration tests that need a DB live next to the package and skip with `t.Skip` if `DATABASE_URL` is not set.
- New code in critical packages (`pki`, `engine`, `webhook`, `provisioner`, `crypto`) requires tests in the same change.

---

## 16. Style and Lint

- `golangci-lint` with the project config; expect to satisfy: `errcheck`, `govet`, `staticcheck`, `gosimple`, `unused`, `ineffassign`, `gosec` (where on), `revive`.
- `gofmt`/`goimports` on save.
- Group imports: stdlib / external / internal — separated by blank lines.
- Avoid named returns unless they materially help readability or are required by `defer`.
- Prefer early return over deep nesting.

---

## 17. Build

- Local: `pnpm run backend:build` (embeds `AGENT_VERSION` via `-ldflags`) or `make build`.
- Production: `apps/backend/Dockerfile` (multi-stage, alpine final).
- Never commit binaries (`apps/backend/bin/` is gitignored).

---

**End of FlowDeploy Backend (Go) Conventions.**
